Final Answer:
##### Mathematical Model

Let $I = \{\text{S1}, \text{S2}, \text{S3}\}$ (stores), $J = \{\text{C1}, \text{C2}, \text{C3}, \text{C4}\}$ (customer groups).

Decision variables:
$$
x_{ij} \geq 0 \quad \text{(continuous)},\quad \forall i \in I,\, j \in J
$$
where $x_{ij}$ is the quantity shipped from store $i$ to customer group $j$.

Parameters:
- $d_j$: demand of customer group $j$ (from customer_demand.csv)
- $s_i$: supply capacity of store $i$ (from supply_capacity.csv)
- $c_{ij}$: transportation cost per unit from store $i$ to customer group $j$ (from transportation_costs.csv)

Objective:
$$
\min \sum_{i \in I} \sum_{j \in J} c_{ij} x_{ij}
$$

Subject to:
1. Demand satisfaction:
$$
\sum_{i \in I} x_{ij} \geq d_j, \quad \forall j \in J
$$

2. Supply capacity:
$$
\sum_{j \in J} x_{ij} \leq s_i, \quad \forall i \in I
$$

3. Non-negativity:
$$
x_{ij} \geq 0, \quad \forall i \in I,\, j \in J
$$

##### Data Mapping

- $I = \{\text{S1}, \text{S2}, \text{S3}\}$ from supply_capacity.csv and transportation_costs.csv row labels.
- $J = \{\text{C1}, \text{C2}, \text{C3}, \text{C4}\}$ from customer_demand.csv and transportation_costs.csv column labels.
- $d_j$ for each $j \in J$ from customer_demand.csv, column "demand".
- $s_i$ for each $i \in I$ from supply_capacity.csv, column "supply_capacity".
- $c_{ij}$ for each $i \in I$, $j \in J$ from transportation_costs.csv, row $i$, column $j$.[0m

